# Check every text file out with LF, on every platform.
#
# The bundled filter corpus (assets/filters/*.toml) carries byte-exact golden
# cases: each `expect` string is compared verbatim against filter output built
# from `\n`. A Windows checkout with autocrlf rewrote those assets to CRLF, so
# all 526 golden cases failed on the windows-latest CI leg while passing on
# Linux — a checkout artifact, not a product bug, but one that makes the corpus
# untestable on Windows.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets must never be touched by line-ending normalization.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.jpeg binary
*.gif binary
*.ico binary
*.pdf binary
*.zip binary
*.gz binary
*.onnx binary
